00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:44.160
outside, which is still hard to do though.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:45.760
You know, uh, it's still hard to do.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:53.380
So I found that like someone like him would probably be good on a team of two, you know,

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:57.160
where you can, you can, you can throw to him when you need to, when you need to like make

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:04.900
a big play. But if you, um, if you're playing like one-on-one with him, I feel like his skillset doesn't

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:10.380
really like help too much because I, you know, I feel like he seemed to miss shots more.

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:17.260
Um, so I feel like there are all this to say, I feel like there are a lot of these statistical

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.840
things that maybe we were saying earlier might've been unbalanced in some one-on-one matchups

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.280
that make it a little more robust and complex.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:29.120
If you're doing two-on-two matchups where you can kind of combine each player's skillset.

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:30.640
They're designed to be complimentary.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:36.220
Yeah. So I didn't play two-on-two, but I did think when I was playing with Bomber that like,

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:40.680
well, maybe I shouldn't have chosen him, but he would be a good teammate or someone, you

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:43.380
know, I know that you're controlling both players, but he would be a good teammate to

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:44.440
like a, a duo.

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:46.500
Yeah. I like, yeah, I agree.

